--- a/TODO.md
+++ b/TODO.md
@@ -23,3 +23,17 @@
 - [ ] `systemPrompterPath` is an untyped string and gets converted with `dbus.ObjectPath(...)` at every use. Type the const as `dbus.ObjectPath`.
 - [ ] `proxy.go:163–166` repeats `newPrompterBridge`'s `(nil, nil)` contract and the reason the fallback is bad. Cut it to the call's purpose.
 - [ ] Doc comments that open with their own name, on unchanged lines: `prompter.go` `prompterBridge`, `BeginPrompting`, `PerformPrompt`, `StopPrompting`, `prompterCallback`, `PromptReady`, `PromptDone`; `prompter_test.go` `mockShellPrompter`, `mockKeyringCallback`, `TestPrompterBridge`; `forward.go` `callForwarder`, `forward`, `nameHasOwner`.
+
+## Unsmell run 2026-11-01 (second pass): prompter bridge cleanup
+
+- [ ] **Possible regression, check first.** `internal/proxy/prompter.go` `newPrompterBridge` now claims SystemPrompter on the backend bus at startup. In remote mode the backend is the user's own session bus. If the proxy starts before gnome-shell registers its prompter (the relogin race), the bridge takes the name on that bus and forwards to the remote side, and gnome-shell then finds the name taken. The deferred activation that this change removed guarded against that. The comment at `prompter.go:63` ("the backend already reaches a real prompter") only holds when gnome-shell is already up. Options: pass the topology (local takeover vs remote) into `newPrompterBridge` and bridge only for local takeover, or restore a watch for remote mode.
+- [ ] `prompter.go` type doc (lines 41–46) and `prompterCallback` doc say the Callback interface is PromptReady only. `prompterCallback` also forwards PromptDone. Fix the type doc, which owns this fact.
+- [ ] One fact, four copies: the exchange payload is forwarded verbatim and the dispatcher never sees the password (`prompter.go` type doc, `PerformPrompt`, `PromptReady`, `forward.go` `callForwarder`). Keep it on `callForwarder` and point to it from the others.
+- [ ] One fact, four copies: gnome-shell owns SystemPrompter on the session bus (`prompter.go` const-block doc, type doc, `frontConn` field comment, `prompter_test.go:14–15`). Keep it on the const block.
+- [ ] `prompter.go` `BeginPrompting` doc narrates in "we" form and leaves out that it errors with ErrFailed when the callback export fails. `PerformPrompt`, `StopPrompting`, `prompterCallback` docs and the `frontConn`/`backendConn` trailing comments and the comment in `unexportCallback` join ideas with semicolons or colons. Rewrite them as plain sentences, together with the name-opening entry above.
+- [ ] `prompter.go` `callbacks map[dbus.ObjectPath]bool` is a set whose value is always true. Use `map[dbus.ObjectPath]struct{}`.
+- [ ] `prompter.go` `prompterCallback.logger` is set in `exportCallback` and never read. Delete it.
+- [ ] `prompter_test.go` hand-rolls a receive with a 5-second timeout three times (`recvCall`, `recvReply`, and the inline select near line 131). Extract one generic `recvWithin[T](t, ch, what)` helper.
+- [ ] `prompter_test.go` `promptCall.sender` is a `string` built as `string(senderOf(msg))` three times. Type it as `senderName` and build it in one helper.
+- [ ] `forward.go` `nameHasOwner` doc explains the prompter bridge's reason for the call. That belongs to the bridge, not to the helper. Cut it to what the function reports.
+- [ ] `e2e/gnome/vm/demo-driver-install.sh`: the comment near line 149 documents a `logout` function that does not exist; the comment near line 62 says `rd_agent` above `rd()`; the un-blank block (esc, idle-delay, ScreenSaver) appears twice (lines ~119 and ~158); `"$HOME/go/bin"` is spelled five times; the "swap in the fixed build until the prompter-bridge fix ships" note is repeated in `demo-driver.sh` and `demo.sh`.
